"""patch_status_g6_pit2.py (2026-10-29): records the measured result of building event_firm_state_pit2 in docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md.
Replaces the G6 sentence that said the usable state would begin about 2007 (wrong) with the measured figures. Gated on the exact installed hash;
each replacement must match exactly once. Usage: python3 scripts/audit/patch_status_g6_pit2.py [docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md]"""
import hashlib, sys
def sha(s): return hashlib.sha256((s if s.endswith("\n") else s + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
p = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md"
S = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
assert sha(S) == "b630d859e707acd9e3344d4aab62cd1a41e5b84c672e0a8363d416a2bf68991c", "PROJECT_STATUS is not the expected version; nothing changed"
def sub(text, old, new, label):
    n = text.count(old); assert n == 1, "%s: expected exactly 1 match, found %d; nothing was written" % (label, n)
    print("ok  ", label); return text.replace(old, new)
S = sub(S, "A join on (security, period_end, form) fixes all 1,790 and moves the usable point-in-time state back to about 2007; 624 rows (93 of them in 2007 to 2010) have no real date and keep the cap LEAST(filed_date, period_end + 90 days). An earlier version of this row said 2006 and 2007 had no filing record and that Q4 rows were untested: both were wrong (the 10-Q-only test missed the Q4 rows, which 10-Ks cover). The values in the early rows still come from later filings and may reflect restatements | open |",
  "624 rows (93 of them in 2007 to 2010) have no real date and keep the cap LEAST(filed_date, period_end + 90 days). **pit_v2 BUILT 10-29** (table event_firm_state_pit2, rule pit_v2; the exact v1 and v2 statements are scripts/sql/event_firm_state_pit_v1_build.sql and event_firm_state_pit_v2_build.sql): availability = the real filing date where sec_filings has one, else the cap. Measured against v1 (23,348 rows each): 21,758 keep the same period, 1,487 gain a period row but only 302 of those have a score (14,176 rows with a state against 13,874: +2.2 percent), 103 get a newer period, none lose a period or fall back, and none change label at the same period; the availability date is never later than the stored one and up to 735 days earlier; 208 states rest on the capped date. The first event with a state moves from 2009-05-21 to 2008-09-25. Two earlier statements in this row were wrong and are replaced: that 2006 and 2007 had no filing record (the 10-Q-only test missed the Q4 rows, which 10-Ks cover) and that the state would begin about 2007 (most 2007 to 2010 statement rows give no composite score). STILL OPEN in G6: report by era and number of terms, then the fate of `diverged`. The values in the early rows still come from later filings and may reflect restatements | open |", "G6 row")
S = sub(S, "Database 3,163 MB, 163 tables and 34 views.\n\n**Numbers recorded in documents", "event_firm_state_pit2 (23,348 rows, rule pit_v2) was created later the same day, after the snapshot of 163 tables and 34 views (3,163 MB): 164 tables since.\n\n**Numbers recorded in documents", "added paragraph")
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(S); print("STATUS sha256", sha(S), "|", S.count("\n"), "lines")